       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (the FDA-labeled maximum). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. Because of that, I'd like to confirm what you intended before I enter anything.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max labeled dose, and may be what you meant.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** If you meant something else, tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nTell me which one you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale for the note field. I'd still advise checking with pharmacy first."
      }
