     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin at 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of a clinical indication that supports it. It carries a real risk of serious harm, mainly lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that, because the ceiling is set by dose-related toxicity. You also haven't given a rationale, which I asked for.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose.\n- **Enter a different dose or frequency** that you choose within the labeled range.\n- **Enter the original order with a note, if you have a documented rationale.** For example, this could be a specific protocol or a recommendation from endocrinology or pharmacy. Send me the rationale and I'll reconsider.\n\nIf the 1,700 mg figure came from a typo or a conversion error, such as confusing a daily total with a per-dose amount, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
